# Visual Studio / .NET Core / ASP.NET Core common ignores

## Build folders
bin/
obj/
artifacts/

## User-specific files
*.user
*.userosscache
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
*.voxe

## Visual Studio workspace
.vs/
.vscode/

## Rider
.idea/
*.sln.iml

## Resharper
_ReSharper*/
*.DotSettings.user

## NuGet packages
*.nupkg
packages/
.nuget/packages/

## Publish output
publish/
publish_temp/
*.Publish.xml
*.azurePubxml

## Runtime / debugging
*.log
logs/
*.vspscc

## ASP.NET / web
wwwroot/lib/    # (optional: if you restore client libs during CI you may want to keep this)
node_modules/
bower_components/

## Configuration / secrets
# Do not commit any personal secret files. If you use a convention such as appsettings.Local.json, ignore it:
appsettings.*.Local.json
secrets.json

## User secrets (stores secrets outside repo by default)
# (No repository entry needed; keep for clarity)
%APPDATA%\Microsoft\UserSecrets/

## Certificate and signing keys
*.pfx
*.snk
*.key

## Database files
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.sqlite
*.db

## Test results / coverage
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

## Tooling
*.vsix
*.nupkg
.vsconfig

## JetBrains Rider caches
.idea/
.idea/*

## Misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
*.backup
*.tmp
*.temp

# End of .gitignore
